<p>Sorry for the necropost (maybe? Idk if a month is a necropost), but, in my headcannon, the original Hanged King's Tragedy was a much older and darker work, stumbled upon and rewritten (as you seem to allude to) by William Cooke (the publisher), which angered 701-1. This would partially explain why William Cooke disappeared and would possibly give 701-1 a reason to want to kill performers of the play.</p>
<p>I'm probably not 100% right on this, and apologies if my breakdown isn't great - I'm writing this around midnight my time and on mobile.</p>

